264
00:14:03,693 --> 00:14:04,600
Go on. Let's go!

265
00:14:04,900 --> 00:14:05,940
Yeah, coming!

266
00:14:06,840 --> 00:14:07,797
But Luffy...

267
00:14:07,880 --> 00:14:09,468
Who is that guy back there?

268
00:14:16,500 --> 00:14:18,500
How did he do that?

269
00:14:32,040 --> 00:14:33,760
Boy, spark!

270
00:14:40,400 --> 00:14:43,200
A fire!

271
00:14:44,060 --> 00:14:45,580
That's no ordinary fire.

272
00:14:47,080 --> 00:14:48,668
What's going on back there?

273
00:14:48,880 --> 00:14:51,351
Looks like a fight between smoke and fire.

274
00:14:51,540 --> 00:14:55,599
So that's the kind of power you get
after eating a flame flame fruit.

275
00:14:56,440 --> 00:14:58,969
Speaking of Devil Fruit,
Luffy, is it true?

276
00:14:59,120 --> 00:15:00,617
Is that guy really your brother?

277
00:15:00,700 --> 00:15:02,080
Yep, his name's Ace.

278
00:15:03,060 --> 00:15:05,897
Look, I'm not surprised to
hear you have a brother, Luffy.

279
00:15:05,980 --> 00:15:08,117
But what's he doing
here on the Grand Line?

280
00:15:08,200 --> 00:15:10,257
Ace is a pirate too, just like I am.

281
00:15:10,340 --> 00:15:14,399
He left home three years before I
did to go search for the One Piece.

282
00:15:19,380 --> 00:15:22,297
Anyway, he bought us some
time, so we can't waste it.

283
00:15:22,380 --> 00:15:23,637
Let's get back to the ship.

284
00:15:23,720 --> 00:15:24,780
Sure, Nami, dear.

285
00:15:30,620 --> 00:15:35,385
Wow, I never would have thought I'd run
into my big brother in a place like this.

286
00:15:37,860 --> 00:15:38,690
Ah!

287
00:15:38,773 --> 00:15:39,603
Which way do we go?

288
00:15:39,686 --> 00:15:41,297
Left, Doosop, everyone get that?

289
00:15:41,380 --> 00:15:43,909
Yes, Nami, I'll follow
you wherever you go.

290
00:15:44,040 --> 00:15:45,920
You close, sick freak. Whoa!

291
00:15:50,220 --> 00:15:53,980
A fight between flame and
smoke is ultimately pointless,

292
00:15:55,160 --> 00:15:57,060
as we've just made obvious.

293
00:15:58,500 --> 00:16:00,559
Where's the Straw Hat and his crew?

294
00:16:00,740 --> 00:16:02,780
They're gone, sir. So is Ace.

295
00:16:02,960 --> 00:16:04,372
We've lost sight of him.

296
00:16:04,720 --> 00:16:09,191
I run into the Straw Hat in the Grand
Line and have him as good as captured.

297
00:16:09,340 --> 00:16:13,040
But then, you just had to get
in my way, didn't you, Ace?

298
00:16:14,420 --> 00:16:15,714
Get everything stowed!

299
00:16:15,820 --> 00:16:17,117
We're shoving off right away!

300
00:16:17,200 --> 00:16:18,030
Aye, aye!

301
00:16:19,120 --> 00:16:20,180
Set the sails!

302
00:16:22,660 --> 00:16:25,200
But it took us so long
to finally get here.

303
00:16:25,380 --> 00:16:27,380
And now we're leaving already, BB?

304
00:16:27,500 --> 00:16:28,477
Yes, but remember,

305
00:16:28,560 --> 00:16:30,457
we only stopped here to
get the supplies we're

306
00:16:30,540 --> 00:16:32,237
going to need for the rest of the journey.

307
00:16:32,320 --> 00:16:33,657
And now that we have all of them,

308
00:16:33,740 --> 00:16:36,957
we're going to head upriver
into the interior of Alabasta.

309
00:16:37,040 --> 00:16:40,160
Our next destination is the
City of Green, Aramaloo.

310
00:16:40,820 --> 00:16:43,220
Aramaloo? Hurry! I am!

311
00:16:43,480 --> 00:16:44,480
Pick up the pace!

312
00:16:44,600 --> 00:16:45,430
Ready!

313
00:16:45,513 --> 00:16:46,720
Right! Set sail!

314
00:16:47,840 --> 00:16:48,670
Huh?

315
00:16:51,660 --> 00:16:52,680
Ah, damn it.

316
00:16:53,000 --> 00:16:56,537
You know, I have the strangest
feeling we're forgetting something.

317
00:16:56,620 --> 00:16:57,450
What the?

318
00:16:57,840 --> 00:16:59,440
Oh, well, that's weird.

319
00:16:59,840 --> 00:17:02,193
I could have sworn they were right here.

320
00:17:05,320 --> 00:17:06,860
But now they're all gone.

321
00:17:07,020 --> 00:17:07,957
Where'd they go?

322
00:17:08,040 --> 00:17:11,452
Well, I guess giving you a
chance to escape was pointless.

323
00:17:12,420 --> 00:17:13,250
Hey!

324
00:17:14,460 --> 00:17:15,440
Hiya, Ace.

325
00:17:17,300 --> 00:17:19,060
It's been a while, hasn't it?

326
00:17:19,360 --> 00:17:20,660
You can say that.

327
00:17:25,720 --> 00:17:27,320
How many years has it been?

328
00:17:27,780 --> 00:17:30,617
I don't know, but you haven't
changed much over that time.

329
00:17:30,700 --> 00:17:33,297
You're a little taller, but
you pretty much look the same.

330
00:17:33,380 --> 00:17:34,210
So do you.

331
00:17:34,380 --> 00:17:36,957
Aside from those powers you got
from eating that Devil Fruit,

332
00:17:37,040 --> 00:17:38,569
you haven't changed a bit.

333
00:17:39,220 --> 00:17:42,477
Remember when you used to sneak into
the fields, eat a hundred watermelons,

334
00:17:42,560 --> 00:17:44,717
spit the seeds out like a
gatling gun and run away?

335
00:17:44,800 --> 00:17:45,737
No, that wasn't me.

336
00:17:45,820 --> 00:17:46,650
That was you.

337
00:17:47,160 --> 00:17:50,297
The farmers would chase you
and you'd scream like a girl.

338
00:17:50,380 --> 00:17:51,357
That was you too.

339
00:17:51,440 --> 00:17:52,800
I watched and laughed.

340
00:18:00,800 --> 00:18:03,500
Guess we're still the same sure are

341
00:18:04,640 --> 00:18:10,620
Just like old times wait wasn't your crew
looking for you a few minutes ago. Yeah.

342
00:18:11,000 --> 00:18:13,353
Hey, what are you doing in this country?

343
00:18:13,520 --> 00:18:15,420
Anyway, I take it.

344
00:18:15,520 --> 00:18:16,757
You never received the message.

345
00:18:16,840 --> 00:18:18,840
I left for you back on drum Island

346
00:18:20,520 --> 00:18:23,340
Well, I guess that's
a no, but don't worry.

347
00:18:23,520 --> 00:18:25,617
It's no big deal It was just to let you

348
00:18:25,700 --> 00:18:28,137
know that I'd be an
Alabasta for a few days.

349
00:18:28,220 --> 00:18:31,557
I'm in these waters on
some business Business huh?

350
00:18:31,640 --> 00:18:35,477
Yeah I'm with the White Beard Pirates.

351
00:18:35,560 --> 00:18:38,957
Catch the White Beard Pirates.

352
00:18:39,040 --> 00:18:40,177
See this tattoo?

353
00:18:40,260 --> 00:18:42,857
That's our mark and it's my pride.

354
00:18:42,940 --> 00:18:49,617
So Luffy, why don't you and your
friends come join us? Come on!

355
00:18:49,700 --> 00:18:50,530
It'll be fun.

356
00:18:50,613 --> 00:18:51,443
What do you say?

357
00:18:51,526 --> 00:18:52,717
No thanks.

358
00:18:52,800 --> 00:18:57,237
I had a feeling you'd say that.

359
00:18:57,320 --> 00:18:58,837
That's too bad because?

360
00:18:58,920 --> 00:19:02,449
But you see, Whitebeard's the
greatest pirate I've ever met.

361
00:19:03,200 --> 00:19:06,637
That's why I'm going to help
him become King of the Pirates.

362
00:19:06,720 --> 00:19:08,960
And not you, Luffy. Sorry.

363
00:19:09,740 --> 00:19:10,570
That's fine.

364
00:19:10,720 --> 00:19:12,955
I guess we'll just have to fight then.

365
00:19:15,020 --> 00:19:17,608
Because I'm going to
be King of the Pirates.

366
00:19:18,840 --> 00:19:19,670
Stop it!

367
00:19:19,753 --> 00:19:20,957
Don't drink at all, you mooch!

368
00:19:21,040 --> 00:19:21,870
Hey!

369
00:19:29,620 --> 00:19:31,797
Something big must be going on in town.

370
00:19:31,880 --> 00:19:33,817
All the Marines on board
wouldn't have left me

371
00:19:33,900 --> 00:19:36,841
and the ship unattended
like this if there wasn't.

372
00:19:37,940 --> 00:19:42,175
Oh, well, whatever it is, it's given
me a perfect opportunity to escape.

373
00:19:43,140 --> 00:19:44,200
Mr. Eleven.

374
00:19:45,320 --> 00:19:47,157
Well, now, since you know my codename,

375
00:19:47,240 --> 00:19:50,037
that can only mean that the three
of you are members of Baroque Works.

376
00:19:50,120 --> 00:19:51,238
I'd guess millions.

377
00:19:51,600 --> 00:19:52,900
Hurry up and untie me.

378
00:19:53,180 --> 00:19:54,677
You're right about one thing.

379
00:19:54,760 --> 00:19:55,997
We're with Baroque Works.

380
00:19:56,080 --> 00:19:58,297
But we're in line to become
number agents, you see.

381
00:19:58,380 --> 00:20:00,439
We're not millions, we're billions.

382
00:20:00,620 --> 00:20:03,797
You are a numbered agent, but looks
like you're barely one at that.

383
00:20:03,880 --> 00:20:06,837
A stronger agent would have never been
captured by the Marines like this.

384
00:20:06,920 --> 00:20:08,449
Can we discuss this later?

385
00:20:08,780 --> 00:20:10,537
Like when I'm not tied up, maybe?

386
00:20:10,620 --> 00:20:13,817
Now help another member out before
all those Marines come back.

387
00:20:13,900 --> 00:20:15,665
Oh, we'll help you, all right.

388
00:20:17,580 --> 00:20:19,960
Right off this mortal coil, that is.

389
00:20:20,420 --> 00:20:25,126
A billions can get promoted to a numbered
agent whenever there's a seat to fill.

390
00:20:25,560 --> 00:20:28,080
And your position is about to be empty.

391
00:20:28,900 --> 00:20:30,580
WAIT! NO! HOLD ON!

392
00:20:37,320 --> 00:20:38,150
HEY!

393
00:20:41,480 --> 00:20:42,697
You won't believe it!

394
00:20:42,780 --> 00:20:44,620
Firefist Ace is here! What?

395
00:20:45,100 --> 00:20:46,060
Firefist Ace?

396
00:20:46,380 --> 00:20:49,817
You mean the second division
commander of the Whitebeard Pirates?

397
00:20:49,900 --> 00:20:52,517
If we can take someone
with his reputation down,

398
00:20:52,600 --> 00:20:55,306
then we're guaranteed
to become number agents.

399
00:20:56,740 --> 00:20:59,120
Here we are You see your ship?

400
00:21:01,400 --> 00:21:03,177
You can't escape from us.

401
00:21:03,260 --> 00:21:04,900
Oh, there it is.

402
00:21:07,320 --> 00:21:09,257
Hey, over here, you guys!

403
00:21:09,340 --> 00:21:10,380
We're here.

404
00:21:11,340 --> 00:21:13,997
Luffy, you go on ahead
and now you already went.

405
00:21:14,080 --> 00:21:16,480
Oh, I don't believe it!

406
00:21:18,620 --> 00:21:19,977
I found Luffy.

407
00:21:20,060 --> 00:21:20,920
Are you sure?

408
00:21:21,420 --> 00:21:24,460
Yeah, that stupid mug is
definitely his. Uh-oh?

409
00:21:28,620 --> 00:21:29,520
Hey, guys!

410
00:21:32,040 --> 00:21:32,920
Lanchi! Tony!

411
00:21:33,180 --> 00:21:34,239
Are you all right?

412
00:21:35,940 --> 00:21:37,540
Oh, Luffy came back!

413
00:21:37,820 --> 00:21:39,040
Yeah, the hard way.

414
00:21:41,000 --> 00:21:42,077
Sorry about that, guys.

415
00:21:42,160 --> 00:21:42,990
My bad.

416
00:21:43,320 --> 00:21:44,617
Yeah, you're sorry, all right.

417
00:21:44,700 --> 00:21:47,857
The sorryest excuse for a captain
who's ever sailed the sea, you moron!

418
00:21:47,940 --> 00:21:50,597
Do you have any idea how much
trouble you've put us in?

419
00:21:50,680 --> 00:21:53,915
Can't you at least try and
act like a captain sometime?

420
00:21:54,060 --> 00:21:54,920
I'm sorry.

421
00:21:55,180 --> 00:21:57,840
Oh, that's right. Where's Ace? Ace?

422
00:21:58,000 --> 00:21:59,765
You're with your brother, huh?

423
00:21:59,980 --> 00:22:00,810
Wait a minute.

424
00:22:00,893 --> 00:22:02,597
You didn't just leave him, did you?

425
00:22:02,680 --> 00:22:04,640
Um, sort of, but don't worry.

426
00:22:05,080 --> 00:22:06,420
Ace is really strong.

427
00:22:06,800 --> 00:22:08,260
So how strong is he?

428
00:22:08,500 --> 00:22:10,037
Well, let me put it like this.

429
00:22:10,120 --> 00:22:12,597
When we were younger, I was never
able to beat him in a fight,

430
00:22:12,680 --> 00:22:16,097
and this was way back in the days
before he ate a flame flame fruit.

431
00:22:16,180 --> 00:22:18,137
That's how strong my big brother is.

432
00:22:18,220 --> 00:22:20,797
You mean there's a flesh-and-blood
person that you couldn't beat?

433
00:22:20,880 --> 00:22:23,917
The big brother of a monster
is an even bigger monster.

434
00:22:24,000 --> 00:22:27,294
I guess so, because Ace used
to beat me up all the time.

435
00:22:27,600 --> 00:22:29,835
But I bet now I can kick his big butt.

436
00:22:30,540 --> 00:22:33,305
I'd like to see you try
and back that claim up.

437
00:22:35,660 --> 00:22:39,200
So, exactly whose butt's getting kicked?

438
00:22:41,320 --> 00:22:42,480
Oh, hey, Ace.

439
00:22:42,620 --> 00:22:44,717
This is my crew I was telling you about.

440
00:22:44,800 --> 00:22:47,537
Nice to meet you, and thanks for
taking care of my kid brother.

441
00:22:47,620 --> 00:22:48,914
I know he's a handful.

442
00:22:49,000 --> 00:22:50,340
Oh, no, not at all.

443
00:22:50,880 --> 00:22:52,040
Come on, be honest.

444
00:22:52,220 --> 00:22:53,737
This is Luffy we're talking about.

445
00:22:53,820 --> 00:22:56,417
Isn't he a bit much for
you to handle at times?

446
00:22:56,500 --> 00:22:57,400
Not at all.

447
00:22:57,660 --> 00:22:58,780
You're good people.

448
00:23:00,360 --> 00:23:01,831
Well, sit down and relax.

449
00:23:01,940 --> 00:23:04,037
I'm sure you two have
lots of catching up to do.

450
00:23:04,120 --> 00:23:05,238
I'll make some tea.

451
00:23:05,420 --> 00:23:08,361
No, that's thoughtful, but
I don't want to impose.

452
00:23:11,920 --> 00:23:13,861
It's not exactly what I expected.

453
00:23:14,260 --> 00:23:15,090
I'll say.

454
00:23:16,540 --> 00:23:19,837
He's polite, helpful, and gracious,
the polar opposite of Luffy.

455
00:23:19,920 --> 00:23:22,357
One of them only cares
about stuffing his face.

456
00:23:22,440 --> 00:23:24,157
There's no way these two can be brothers.

457
00:23:24,240 --> 00:23:26,277
Well, the other only
cares about his brother.

458
00:23:26,360 --> 00:23:28,757
I wish I had a wonderful
brother like that.

459
00:23:28,840 --> 00:23:31,777
Brother, I wish I had a
wonderful captain like that.

460
00:23:31,860 --> 00:23:33,180
Saatchi, he's kidding.

461
00:23:33,500 --> 00:23:35,735
See, I told you they were interesting.

462
00:23:40,200 --> 00:23:42,788
Baroque Works, those
are the Billions ships.

463
00:23:43,000 --> 00:23:45,757
Are we going to let them
escape from the Billions?

464
00:23:45,840 --> 00:23:46,820
No way!

465
00:23:47,960 --> 00:23:51,677
Hey, we'll show him what Baroque works
billions are made of, full speed ahead!

466
00:23:51,760 --> 00:23:52,880
Those guys again?

467
00:23:53,220 --> 00:23:56,320
Luffy, leave it to me, I'll handle it.

468
00:23:58,540 --> 00:24:00,120
He's going all by himself?

469
00:24:00,420 --> 00:24:02,160
And in that dinky bow, too.

470
00:24:04,120 --> 00:24:06,357
I wouldn't worry about him if I were you.

471
00:24:06,440 --> 00:24:08,037
They don't let just
anyone become the second

472
00:24:08,120 --> 00:24:10,417
division commander of
the Whitebeard Pirates.

473
00:24:10,500 --> 00:24:11,660
Is he insane?

474
00:24:12,160 --> 00:24:14,097
Firefest is heading right towards us.

475
00:24:14,180 --> 00:24:15,010
Let him come!

476
00:24:15,093 --> 00:24:17,960
Our ships are going to make
matchsticks out of his.

477
00:24:20,600 --> 00:24:21,640
He jumped!

478
00:24:22,160 --> 00:24:23,360
Open fire!

479
00:24:23,740 --> 00:24:25,460
Throw him to pieces, men!

480
00:24:36,340 --> 00:24:37,740
Fire fist!

481
00:24:59,340 --> 00:25:02,160
He roasted them!

482
00:25:14,180 --> 00:25:15,062
Captain Smoker,

483
00:25:15,260 --> 00:25:17,717
we've combed the entire city, sir,

484
00:25:17,800 --> 00:25:20,317
but Straw Hat Luffy and his
crew are nowhere to be found.

485
00:25:20,400 --> 00:25:22,753
Do you want to know who I saw with them?

486
00:25:23,600 --> 00:25:25,835
Vivi, and I'm certain it was her, too.

487
00:25:26,260 --> 00:25:27,090
Vivi?

488
00:25:27,173 --> 00:25:28,577
As in Princess Vivi Nefertari?

489
00:25:28,660 --> 00:25:30,657
But what would she be doing
with the Straw Hat pirates?

490
00:25:30,740 --> 00:25:32,280
She must be their hostage.

491
00:25:32,600 --> 00:25:36,777
They probably abducted her in the hopes
that her father would pay a hefty ransom.

492
00:25:36,860 --> 00:25:37,690
Doubt it.

493
00:25:37,773 --> 00:25:41,017
She wasn't acting like a kidnapped
victim, more like part of the crew.

494
00:25:41,100 --> 00:25:44,020
The princess acting like a pirate?

495
00:25:45,080 --> 00:25:46,817
Something strange is happening.

496
00:25:46,900 --> 00:25:48,724
I just wish I knew what it was.

497
00:25:49,360 --> 00:25:50,242
Captain Smoker!

498
00:25:50,600 --> 00:25:53,120
I'm sorry, sir, but it appears that Mr.

499
00:25:53,260 --> 00:25:56,697
Eleven was killed on board the ship while
we were off searching for the Straw Hats,

500
00:25:56,780 --> 00:25:59,237
who, by the way, we still
haven't located yet.

501
00:25:59,320 --> 00:26:01,277
Call off the search for Straw Hat Luffy.

502
00:26:01,360 --> 00:26:03,717
I have a pretty good
idea where he's headed.

503
00:26:03,800 --> 00:26:06,160
He's after Crocodile. I'm sure of it.

504
00:26:06,640 --> 00:26:07,680
Why Crocodile?

505
00:26:08,060 --> 00:26:10,497
He's one of the seven warlords of the sea.

506
00:26:10,580 --> 00:26:12,639
A pirate given government approval.

507
00:26:12,860 --> 00:26:17,660
I find all of the seven warlords despicable,
but Crocodile's the absolute worst.

508
00:26:18,040 --> 00:26:22,617
Politically speaking, isn't he an ally
of the world government and the Marines?

509
00:26:22,700 --> 00:26:25,637
Crocodile might have the powers
that be fooled, but not me.

510
00:26:25,720 --> 00:26:29,237
They're delusional if they think giving
him a sanction will make him obey.

511
00:26:29,320 --> 00:26:30,150
He's a pirate.

512
00:26:30,300 --> 00:26:32,917
There's one thing you always
need to remember, Tashigi.

513
00:26:33,000 --> 00:26:35,437
A pirate's a pirate no
matter where they go.

514
00:26:35,520 --> 00:26:36,860
They never change.

515
00:26:38,260 --> 00:26:40,197
Crocodile will lead us right to him.

516
00:26:40,280 --> 00:26:42,017
Straw Hat will show up wherever he is.

517
00:26:42,100 --> 00:26:45,137
And I'm sure we'll find out
what's going on when we get there.

518
00:26:45,220 --> 00:26:47,900
There'll be no escape
for him. Not this time.

